<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 6/3/97		  27/2/97		8/3/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    550		  475-500	     600-625</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100		   75-100		    75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,750	    1,650-1,750	 1,750-1,775</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    375			400	     350-375</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  15-20			 25		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose despite some product heading for Germany and out of the region in cargoes.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were steady. Some product arrived in cargoes and left as barges or by pipe.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks rose with arrivals from the FSU, despite some rapid throughput to the continental hinterland.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks were also up with product from the FSU. Some material left as VGO to Germany, but the poor bunker market drew little cracked fuel oil away.</p>
<p>Jet fuel fell as product departed to the gas oil sector and a couple of barges went to the aviation industry.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
